**Alarmo events**

- Alarm triggered: {triggered}
- Entry delay: {pending}
- Exit delay: {arming}
- Armed: {armed}
- Disarmed: {disarmed}
- Failed to arm: {failed_to_arm}

**Sensors**

{sensors}

Shows Home Assistant opening sensors and any other sensors with saved rules, not the list of sensors linked to Alarmo.

— = No sound assigned. P0 = Low, P1 = Normal, P2 = High, P3 = Critical. ↻ = Repeat.

Each sensor shows its playback conditions. Always mode works without Alarmo; disarmed mode and failed arming require a linked panel. Use the buttons below to view or edit an event or sensor selection.

**Speech alerts**

{speech}

speech_rule.description:
Sensor: {sensor}. {status}

Speech is: before text + current value + optional unit + after text. Example: “The room temperature is” + 22 + “degrees Celsius” (after text, with unit disabled). No YAML or templates. Uses the engine default voice/language.

Test without saving reads the current value; choose Save afterwards to keep edits. Thresholds trigger only on crossing. The minimum interval drops frequent alerts. Unavailable states, startup and reconnection are ignored. Manual mode exposes the JackSignal · Speak sensor value action for any automation.

dlna_status.description:
**Current state** (✓ active / — inactive)

- HTTP receiver: {running}
- SSDP discovery: {discovery}
- Description: {url}
- Audio active: {playback} · Priority: {priority}
- Last HTTP request (UTC time, IP, method, result): {last_request}
- Last observed DLNA error: {last_error}

Select DLNA diagnostics to refresh. Data resets when the integration reloads. Enabled SSDP does not prove the phone receives announcements. The last request may come from a browser rather than a controller. Audio URLs and credentials are not displayed.

Use an app supporting DLNA renderers, such as BubbleUPnP. VPN multicast discovery typically needs additional configuration.
